---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const tour = [
  {
    image: '/images/products/visionstudio-initiatives.webp',
    width: 1317,
    height: 883,
    alt: 'VisionStudio All Initiatives view: initiatives grouped by program — Market-Spec, OmniAgent on Lightsail, PRISM Control — as cards with initiative IDs, status badges, and completion bars, beside a portfolio summary of completed, proposed, in-progress, and cancelled counts',
    title: 'Initiative Portfolio',
    description:
      'The whole book of work at a glance. Every initiative rolls up under its program, each card carrying a stable initiative ID, a lifecycle status — delivery complete, executing, proposed — and a live completion bar. A summary ring tallies the portfolio: completed, in progress, proposed, and cancelled.',
  },
  {
    image: '/images/products/visionstudio-program.webp',
    width: 1319,
    height: 877,
    alt: 'PRISM Control program view showing its eight initiatives as a card grid with IDs, status badges, and per-initiative completion, plus a program-level summary of roadmap-item counts by state',
    title: 'Programs & Roadmap',
    description:
      'Drill into a single program — here PRISM Control — to see just its initiatives and their roadmap items (RMIs). Program-level counts summarize how much is delivered, ready, proposed, or cancelled, so an owner can triage one program without losing sight of the rest.',
  },
  {
    image: '/images/products/visionstudio-initiative-definition.webp',
    width: 1318,
    height: 882,
    alt: "An initiative's Definition Details tab: a PBHQ-Lite spec pipeline — PRD, TRD, PLAN, ROADMAP — with a per-stage LLM-as-a-Judge score out of five, an average score, and the selected spec's markdown rendered below",
    title: 'Spec Definition + LLM-as-a-Judge',
    description:
      'Each initiative is defined as a chain of specs — PRD, TRD, PLAN, ROADMAP in the PBHQ-Lite workflow — and every stage is judged in place, carrying a categorical score out of five. The weakest link (a ROADMAP at 3/5 here) is obvious at a glance, and the spec’s rendered markdown sits right below it for revision.',
  },
  {
    image: '/images/products/visionstudio-initiative-execution.webp',
    width: 1319,
    height: 884,
    alt: "The same initiative's Execution Details tab: an RMI status summary and a Foundation phase expanded to list individual roadmap items with completion badges and dependency links",
    title: 'Execution Tracking',
    description:
      'From spec to shipped: the Execution tab tracks the initiative’s roadmap items (RMIs) grouped into phases, each RMI with a completion status and its dependencies. Per-phase progress bars show how far Foundation — and everything built on top of it — has actually gotten.',
  },
  {
    image: '/images/products/visionstudio-performance.webp',
    width: 1321,
    height: 884,
    alt: 'VisionStudio Performance dashboard: headline totals for tokens, input, output, cache reads, and cost; pie charts breaking tokens and cost down by model and by category; and weekly spend-over-time bar charts',
    title: 'Performance & Token Economics',
    description:
      'The build has a bill. The Performance dashboard surfaces total tokens, cache reads, and cost, then breaks them down by model and by category — input, output, cache — with spend-over-time trends. Cache reads dominating the token mix is the tell that context reuse is doing its job.',
  },
  {
    image: '/images/products/visionstudio-performance-monthly.webp',
    width: 1322,
    height: 888,
    alt: 'Performance monthly history: a month summary of cost and tokens, a cost-by-model pie, a month-over-month table with tokens, cost, and percentage change, and an accomplishments count with a weekly velocity chart',
    title: 'Monthly Trends & Accomplishments',
    description:
      'Zoom out to the month. A running history compares cost and token volume period over period, ties spend back to the models that drove it, and pairs it with what actually shipped — an accomplishments count and weekly velocity — so cost is always read against output, never in isolation.',
  },
]
---

<BaseLayout title="VisionStudio">
  <div class="py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-8">
      <span class="text-xs font-medium px-2 py-1 bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-[var(--color-primary-dark)] rounded">PBHQ Original</span>
      <span class="text-xs font-medium px-2 py-1 bg-[var(--color-primary)]/10 text-[var(--color-primary)] rounded">Tool</span>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mt-4 mb-6">VisionStudio</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mb-8">
        An LLM-powered web application for authoring, evaluating, and executing product
        specifications — an integrated workspace that carries the VisionSpec methodology from
        first draft through LLM-as-a-Judge review to tracked, shipped execution.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12 mb-4">Key Capabilities</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-4 text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">
        <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">Dual methodology selection:</strong> choose a requirements methodology (AWS Working Backwards, and others) and an implementation methodology (AIDLC, SpecKit) per project.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">LLM-as-a-Judge evaluation:</strong> evaluate specs against profile rubrics, with a context-aware writing assistant to help close the gaps it finds.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">AIDLC workflow:</strong> AWS's AI-Driven Development Lifecycle — Inception → Construction → Operations — with generated deliverables and phase gates to track completion.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">Initiative &amp; portfolio execution:</strong> track initiatives, phases, and stable roadmap items (RMIs) across programs and repositories, with per-phase completion — surfaced from PRISM.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">Strategic planning:</strong> V2MOM cascades from organization to team to project, a visual capability stack, and a timeline roadmap view.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">Maturity Model dashboards:</strong> framework-based maturity assessments, including <a href="/products/scale" class="text-[var(--color-primary)] hover:underline">SCALE</a>.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">Performance &amp; token economics:</strong> tokens, cost, and cache usage broken down by model, category, and month, with month-over-month trends and shipped-work velocity — alongside DevX signals from OmniDevX.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-8 mt-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-10 max-w-4xl">Product Tour</h2>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-16">
        {tour.map((stop, index) => (
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 items-center">
            <div class:list={['rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-[var(--color-border)] shadow-xl', index % 2 === 1 && 'md:order-2']}>
              <img src={stop.image} alt={stop.alt} width={stop.width} height={stop.height} loading="lazy" class="w-full h-auto block" />
            </div>
            <div class:list={[index % 2 === 1 && 'md:order-1']}>
              <span class="block font-mono text-sm text-[var(--color-text-subtle)] mb-3">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3 text-[var(--color-text)]">{stop.title}</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)] leading-relaxed m-0">{stop.description}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-8 mt-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Why It Matters</h2>
      <p class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">
        As AI compresses the distance between intent and implementation, the bottleneck moves
        upstream — to how well a spec is written and judged before an agent ever touches code.
        VisionStudio is the applied tool for the <a href="/frameworks/spec-driven-development#visionspec" class="text-[var(--color-primary)] hover:underline">VisionSpec methodology</a>
        described on this site: it turns strategy, specifications, and delivery workflows into an
        operating system a ProductBuilder can actually run.
      </p>

      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 mt-10">
        <a href="https://github.com/ProductBuildersHQ/visionstudio" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-6 py-3 bg-[var(--color-primary-dark)] text-white font-medium rounded-lg no-underline hover:bg-[var(--color-primary)] transition-colors">View on GitHub</a>
        <a href="/visionstudio/" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-6 py-3 bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-[var(--color-primary-dark)] font-medium rounded-lg no-underline hover:bg-[var(--color-accent-light)] transition-colors">Documentation</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
